CLINICAL REASONING SUMMARY

Patient presented with rapidly evolving systemic symptoms consistent with delayed IgE-mediated hypersensitivity. The presence of tachycardia, relative hypotension, and widespread urticaria necessitated immediate after-hours physical assessment to determine the need for intramuscular adrenaline and to establish airway security. Deferring review until standard clinic hours posed an unacceptable risk of profound anaphylactic shock and fatal airway compromise. Intervention and clinical stabilization were urgently required in the home environment.

